            <div class="eyebrow">Why we’re building LIMA</div>
            <h1>A physical foundation<br>for molecular discovery.</h1>
            <p>LIMA Dynamics was conceived to empower researchers working to understand and treat complex diseases with advances in artificial intelligence and machine learning.</p>
            <h2>Generative AI in drug discovery</h2>
            <p>In classical drug discovery, researchers search known compounds for a desired effect on a target protein. Inverse molecular design takes a different approach: specify the desired behavior, then use generative AI to propose molecules that could achieve it.</p>
            <p>Those proposals need a physical foundation. A simulation engine can help researchers explore molecular interactions and generate data for evaluating and improving their models.</p>
            <h2>Where LIMA fits</h2>
            <p>LIMA MD is a molecular dynamics engine built for modern research and agent workflows. It uses NVIDIA GPUs to simulate molecular systems and supports workflows for building membranes, preparing structures, and running simulations.</p>
            <p>Our ambition is to give researchers and AI systems an accessible physical simulation engine—a digital laboratory for exploring molecular interactions.</p>
